    "q-81346": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81346",
      "name": "Question 13",
      "problem": "Calculate ${\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{x}^{2}-2}^{2-2{x}^{2}}6{x}^{3}\\,dy\\,dx.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{-{x}^{2}-2}^{2-2{x}^{2}}6{x}^{3}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{3}[{\\int }_{-{x}^{2}-2}^{2-2{x}^{2}}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}6{x}^{3}(2-2{x}^{2}-(-{x}^{2}-2))dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(-6{x}^{5}+24{x}^{3})\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(24{x}^{3}-6{x}^{5})\\,dx & ={[6{x}^{4}-{x}^{6}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =(6-1)-0 \\\\  & =5\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
