    "q-37864": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37864",
      "name": "Question 15",
      "problem": "${\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx=$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over a type I region.\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}{x}^{5}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}[y]_{\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}^{1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x}\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}((1+\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)-\\operatorname{sin}⁡x)\\,dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{2\\pi }{x}^{5}\\,dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{6}}{6}]}_{0}^{2\\pi } \\\\  & =\\frac{(2\\pi )^{6}}{6}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{32{\\pi }^{6}}{3}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
