      "kp_id": "e-7027"
    },
    "q-81774": {
      "dom_id": "step-q81774",
      "name": "Question 17",
      "problem": "Calculate ${∬}_{D}x\\,dA,\\,$\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over the type I region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,0\\le x\\le 1,\\,2{x}^{2}\\le y\\le {x}^{2}+1\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}x\\,dA & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}x\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[{\\int }_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x[y]_{2{x}^{2}}^{{x}^{2}+1}dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x({x}^{2}+1-2{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}x(1-{x}^{2})dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{0}^{1}(x-{x}^{3})dx & ={[\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}-\\frac{{x}^{4}}{4}]}_{0}^{1} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}-\\frac{1}{4}-0 \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
