    "q-37684": {
      "dom_id": "step-q37684",
      "name": "Question 20",
      "problem": "Calculate ${∬}_{D}\\frac{{e}^{2y}}{x}\\,dA,$\nwhere $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 3\\}.$",
      "worked_solution": "The integral is defined over the type I region $D=\\{(x,y)\\,:\\,1\\le x\\le 5,\\,\\operatorname{ln}⁡x\\le y\\le 3\\}.$\n\nSo, we can express the integral as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{∬}_{D}\\frac{{e}^{2y}}{x}\\,dA & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{2y}}{x}\\,dy\\,dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nFirst, we evaluate the inner integral by integrating with respect to $y$, treating $x$ as a constant:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{\\int }_{1}^{5}{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{3}\\frac{{e}^{2y}}{x}\\,dy\\,dx & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}[{\\int }_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{3}{e}^{2y}\\,dy]dx \\\\  & ={\\int }_{1}^{5}\\frac{1}{x}{[\\frac{1}{2}{e}^{2y}]}_{\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}^{3}dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{{e}^{6}}{x}-\\frac{{e}^{2\\operatorname{ln}⁡x}}{x})dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{{e}^{6}}{x}-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{x})dx \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{{e}^{6}}{x}-x)dx\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nThen, we integrate with respect to $x:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}\\frac{1}{2}{\\int }_{1}^{5}(\\frac{{e}^{6}}{x}-x)dx & =\\frac{1}{2}{[{e}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡x-\\frac{{x}^{2}}{2}]}_{1}^{5} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{2}(({e}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(5)-\\frac{25}{2})-({e}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡(1)-\\frac{1}{2})) \\\\  & =\\frac{{e}^{6}\\operatorname{ln}⁡5}{2}-6\\end{aligned}\n$$",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-37684-a",
